{"assets":["/editorial-assets/2f7f89932ff7170f25147799e497b44229205e7a2c8f70fd90c4f591e30d2930.png","/editorial-assets/991f18b67c389d759eafcede8794280a83f13119c37b852077f07d457c8d1f22.png","/editorial-assets/45ffc5a0785b71dd034b1787bbd53bd019d7a00412ea7e1c0882c429c6fc1ab2.png"],"contestId":"41","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"I wrote this post to help my friend , Iman Movahhedi , complete "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://www.codeforces.com/blog/entry/1492"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"this one"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Round #40 was my first contest here in Codeforces and I feel I fell in love with CF just after that."},{"kind":"line_break"},{"kind":"horizontal_rule"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A-Translation: "}],"kind":"strong"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"attrs":{"href":"http://pastebin.com/YmxXqAAS"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"C# code"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":")"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Many languages have built-in reverse() function for strings. we can reverse one of the strings and check if it's equal to the other one , or we can check it manually. I prefer the second. "}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"horizontal_rule"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"B-Martian Dollar: "}],"kind":"strong"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"attrs":{"href":"http://pastebin.com/EP3KPzUf"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"C# code"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Since number of days is very small (2 × 10"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"3"}],"kind":"superscript"},{"kind":"text","text":") we can just iterate over all possibilities of buy-day and sell-day. This will take θ ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"2"}],"kind":"superscript"},{"kind":"text","text":") time which is OK."}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"horizontal_rule"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"C-Email Address: "}],"kind":"strong"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"attrs":{"href":"http://pastebin.com/mfbkckEU"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"C++ code"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first letter of the input string can not be part of an \"at\" or a \"dot\" so we start from the second character. Greedily put \".\" wherever you reached \"dot\" and put \"@\" the first time you reached \"at\". This will take θ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":") time , where "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" is the length of input."}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"horizontal_rule"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"D-Pawn:"}],"kind":"strong"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each cell of the table store "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" + 1 values. Where "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"th value is the maximum number of peas the pawn can take while he is at that cell and this number mod "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" + 1 is "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"This makes a "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"2"}],"kind":"superscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" × "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"m"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" × "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":") dynamic programming which fits perfectly in the time."}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"horizontal_rule"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"E-3-cycles: "}],"kind":"strong"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"attrs":{"href":"http://pastebin.com/Z90p9BAm"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"C++ code"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The road map with most edges is a complete bipartite graph with equal number of vertices on each side. (Prove it by yourself :D ). We can make such a graph by putting the first "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/2f7f89932ff7170f25147799e497b44229205e7a2c8f70fd90c4f591e30d2930.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":" vertices on one side and the other "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/991f18b67c389d759eafcede8794280a83f13119c37b852077f07d457c8d1f22.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":" on the other side.For sure , number of edges is "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/45ffc5a0785b71dd034b1787bbd53bd019d7a00412ea7e1c0882c429c6fc1ab2.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"line_break"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"container"}],"kind":"document"},"schema":2,"sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/blog/entry/1620"}